 "summary": "An amber caution: the flight controls are in direct law. Sidestick deflection moves the surfaces directly, there is no automatic trim (USE MAN PITCH TRIM on the PFD) and no protection. Overspeed and stall warnings remain. Keep below 320 kt / M .77, trim manually, use small inputs at high speed, prefer manual thrust and avoid large thrust changes. Land in CONF 3 at VREF + 10 kt.",
